---
import { Card, Icon } from '@santi020k/lumen-astro'

import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
---

<Base
  title="Architecture"
  description="Follow Way’s guidance from versioned Markdown to a validated local catalog, agent plugins, and the website. See what each part owns and what stays on your machine."
>
  <header class="page-intro architecture-intro">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Architecture / How Way fits together</p>
      <h1>
        One source.
        <br />
        <em>Several ways in.</em>
      </h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Write the guidance once. Build a shared catalog. Read it on the web or
        bring it into your agent, with the same decisions behind every entry point.
      </p>
      <a class="text-action" href="#guidance-flow">
        Follow the guidance <Icon name="arrow-down" aria-hidden="true" />
      </a>
    </div>
    <aside class="architecture-summary" aria-label="At a glance">
      <p class="tiny-label">Shared guidance, clear boundaries</p>
      <dl>
        <div>
          <dt>Versioned sources</dt>
          <dd>Markdown and source metadata in Git.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Local retrieval</dt>
          <dd>A packaged catalog, with no hosted search service.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Deliberate updates</dt>
          <dd>Preview changes. Keep a recovery path.</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </aside>
  </header>

  <section id="guidance-flow" class="architecture-map" aria-labelledby="flow-title">
    <div class="architecture-map-heading">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">From source to reference</p>
        <h2 id="flow-title">One build. Shared context.</h2>
      </div>
      <p>Turborepo builds the catalog before its plugin and website consumers.</p>
    </div>
    <ol class="architecture-stages">
      <li>
        <Card class="architecture-stage">
          <p class="tiny-label"><span>01</span> / Author</p>
          <h3>Standards & decisions</h3>
          <p>
            The owning Markdown files hold the guidance. The catalog index
            records each reference’s scope, source, tags, and review date.
          </p>
          <div class="architecture-paths">
            <code>standards/ + docs/</code>
            <code>standards/catalog.json</code>
          </div>
          <p class="architecture-stage-note">Edit the owning source.</p>
        </Card>
        <span class="architecture-connector" aria-hidden="true">
          <Icon name="arrow-right" />
        </span>
      </li>
      <li>
        <Card class="architecture-stage architecture-stage-core">
          <p class="tiny-label"><span>02</span> / Build</p>
          <h3>A validated catalog</h3>
          <p>
            The shared package validates metadata and content hashes. Its CLI
            and read-only MCP server search and retrieve the packaged references.
          </p>
          <div class="architecture-paths">
            <code>@santi020k/way</code>
            <code>packages/way/</code>
          </div>
          <p class="architecture-stage-note">Generate outputs; keep sources authoritative.</p>
        </Card>
        <span class="architecture-connector" aria-hidden="true">
          <Icon name="arrow-right" />
        </span>
      </li>
      <li>
        <Card class="architecture-stage">
          <p class="tiny-label"><span>03</span> / Use</p>
          <h3>Choose your entry point</h3>
          <ul class="architecture-destinations">
            <li>
              <strong>Codex & Claude Code</strong>
              <span>Generated plugins with skills and local MCP retrieval.</span>
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>The website</strong>
              <span>Readable, searchable references from the same catalog.</span>
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Global instructions</strong>
              <span>Managed separately through explicit CLI setup.</span>
            </li>
          </ul>
          <p class="architecture-stage-note">Adapt delivery to each host.</p>
        </Card>
      </li>
    </ol>
    <p class="architecture-map-caption">
      <Icon name="arrow-up-right" aria-hidden="true" />
      Theme owns brand tokens. Lumen owns component contracts. Way points to
      those sources; current repository evidence takes precedence over snapshots.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="boundaries-title">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">Access & ownership</p>
      <h2 id="boundaries-title">Read freely.<br /> Change deliberately.</h2>
      <p>
        Looking up a standard and installing instructions are separate operations.
        Your agent’s runtime configuration stays under your control.
      </p>
    </div>
    <dl class="architecture-boundaries">
      <div>
        <dt><Icon name="search" aria-hidden="true" /> Search & retrieve</dt>
        <dd>
          The MCP reads the packaged catalog. It does not read arbitrary files
          or change your agent’s configuration.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt><Icon name="terminal" aria-hidden="true" /> Preview & install</dt>
        <dd>
          CLI setup requires the exact preview hash before writing managed
          instructions and versioned references. It preserves surrounding text
          and retains a private backup receipt.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt><Icon name="shield-check" aria-hidden="true" /> Keep local control</dt>
        <dd>
          Models, permissions, trusted directories, credentials, and history stay
          outside setup’s write scope. Rollback refuses to erase later instruction edits.
        </dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="decisions-title">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">The reasoning behind the system</p>
      <h2 id="decisions-title">Decisions you<br /> can inspect.</h2>
      <p>Read the context, alternatives, and consequences behind these boundaries.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="area-list">
      <a class="area-row" href="/standards/0001-shared-sources/">
        <span class="row-number">01</span>
        <div>
          <p class="tiny-label">Accepted decision</p>
          <h3>Share sources; adapt delivery.</h3>
          <p>
            Why the catalog is local, the plugins are generated, and Lumen keeps
            its component contracts.
          </p>
        </div>
        <Icon name="arrow-up-right" aria-hidden="true" />
      </a>
      <a class="area-row" href="/standards/0002-local-configuration/">
        <span class="row-number">02</span>
        <div>
          <p class="tiny-label">Accepted decision</p>
          <h3>Keep machine configuration local.</h3>
          <p>
            Why a guidance update preserves your settings, requires an exact
            preview, and keeps a recovery receipt.
          </p>
        </div>
        <Icon name="arrow-up-right" aria-hidden="true" />
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
  <div class="architecture-next">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Put the architecture to work</p>
      <h2>Start with a preview.</h2>
    </div>
    <a class="text-action" href="/start/">
      Set up your agent <Icon name="arrow-right" aria-hidden="true" />
    </a>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .section {
    padding-block: 4.5rem;
  }
  .section > * {
    min-width: 0;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }
  .area-row {
    grid-template-columns: 1.5rem minmax(0, 1fr) 1.1rem;
  }
  .text-action .ui-icon {
    width: 1.1rem;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }
  .architecture-intro {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.5fr) minmax(0, 0.8fr);
    align-items: center;
    gap: 5rem;
  }
  .architecture-intro .text-action {
    margin-top: 1.4rem;
  }
  .architecture-summary {
    border-left: 1px solid var(--site-line);
    padding-left: 2rem;
  }
  .architecture-summary dl {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.2rem;
    margin: 1.5rem 0 0;
  }
  .architecture-summary dt {
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .architecture-summary dd {
    margin: 0.25rem 0 0;
    color: var(--site-ink-soft);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
  }
  .architecture-map {
    padding-block: 2rem 0;
    scroll-margin-top: 7rem;
  }
  .architecture-map-heading {
    display: flex;
    align-items: end;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }
  .architecture-map-heading .eyebrow {
    margin-bottom: 0.8rem;
  }
  .architecture-map-heading h2,
  .architecture-next h2 {
    font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 3vw, 2.4rem);
  }
  .architecture-map-heading > p {
    max-width: 20rem;
    color: var(--site-ink-soft);
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
  }
  .architecture-stages {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 2.5rem;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }
  .architecture-stages > li {
    position: relative;
    min-width: 0;
  }
  .architecture-stage {
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
    height: 100%;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    padding: 1.6rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--site-line);
    border-radius: 1.2rem;
    background: var(--site-surface);
    color: var(--site-ink);
    box-shadow: none;
  }
  .architecture-stage-core {
    border-color: var(--site-accent);
  }
  .architecture-stage .tiny-label span {
    color: var(--site-accent);
  }
  .architecture-stage h3 {
    margin-block: 1.2rem 0.85rem;
    font-size: 1.25rem;
  }
  .architecture-stage > p:not(.tiny-label),
  .architecture-destinations {
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    color: var(--site-ink-soft);
  }
  .architecture-paths {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.4rem;
    margin-block: 1.2rem;
    color: var(--site-accent);
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }
  .architecture-stage > .architecture-stage-note {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--site-line);
    padding-top: 1rem;
    margin-top: auto;
    font-size: 0.6875rem;
  }
  .architecture-connector {
    position: absolute;
    left: 100%;
    top: 50%;
    width: 2.5rem;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    color: var(--site-accent);
  }
  .architecture-destinations {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0 0 1.2rem;
  }
  .architecture-destinations strong,
  .architecture-destinations span {
    display: block;
  }
  .architecture-destinations strong {
    color: var(--site-ink);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .architecture-destinations span {
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    margin-top: 0.25rem;
  }
  .architecture-map-caption {
    display: flex;
    align-items: start;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    color: var(--site-ink-soft);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    max-width: 49rem;
  }
  .architecture-map-caption .ui-icon {
    color: var(--site-accent);
    margin-top: 0.15rem;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }
  .architecture-boundaries {
    margin: 0;
  }
  .architecture-boundaries > div + div {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--site-line);
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    padding-top: 1.5rem;
  }
  .architecture-boundaries dt {
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    align-items: center;
    font-size: 1rem;
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  .architecture-boundaries .ui-icon {
    color: var(--site-accent);
  }
  .architecture-boundaries dd {
    margin: 0.65rem 0 0 1.85rem;
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    color: var(--site-ink-soft);
  }
  .architecture-next {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 2rem;
    padding-block: 3rem;
  }
  .architecture-next .eyebrow {
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }
  @media (max-width: 950px) {
    .architecture-intro {
      gap: 2rem;
    }
    .architecture-stages {
      gap: 1.75rem;
    }
    .architecture-stage {
      padding: 1.25rem;
    }
    .architecture-connector {
      width: 1.75rem;
    }
  }
  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .architecture-intro {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 2.5rem;
      padding-bottom: 2rem;
    }
    .architecture-summary {
      padding-left: 1.25rem;
    }
    .architecture-map-heading {
      align-items: start;
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 1rem;
    }
    .architecture-map-heading > p {
      max-width: 100%;
    }
    .architecture-stages {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 2.5rem;
    }
    .architecture-stage {
      padding: 1.5rem;
    }
    .architecture-connector {
      top: 100%;
      left: calc(50% - 1.25rem);
      width: 2.5rem;
      height: 2.5rem;
      align-items: center;
      transform: rotate(90deg);
    }
    .architecture-next {
      flex-direction: column;
      align-items: start;
      gap: 1rem;
    }
  }
</style>
